  "subject": "🎸 Axios Finish Line: Fan letters",
  "date": "Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:29:28 -0500",
  "body_text": "96 \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n 🦫 Plus: Beaver Moon | Wednesday, November 25, 2026 \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n View in browser \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n PRESENTED BY AMAZON \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n Axios Finish Line \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n By Mike Allen and Erica Pandey and Jim VandeHei &middot; Nov 25, 2026 \r\n \r\n \r\n 🥧 Happy Thanksgiving Eve! Axios Nashville's Adam Tamburin is your host this evening, with a lesson on the joy of expressing gratitude — even when you're not expecting anything in return.\n\n Smart Brevity™ count: 394 words … 1½ mins. Copy edited by Amy Stern. \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n 1 big thing: Write fan mail \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n Fans gather by a mural to pay respects to Dolly Parton in Knoxville, Tenn., after her death was announced in August. Photo: Megan Varner/Reuters When Dolly Parton died in August, the sadness I felt didn't surprise me. What I didn't expect was the wave of regret that hit me next, Axios Nashville's Adam Tamburin writes. \n\n Flashback: I thought for years about thanking her for the ways her work enriched my life. But I stopped short of dropping a fan letter in the mail. In some ways it felt silly: How much could one person's note matter to her? She'd probably never even see it. 🦋 But after she died, I realized how much sharing my gratitude would have mattered to me. I wish I had made the effort, regardless of the outcome.\n\n So this fall, I decided to start making the effort and began sending fan mail for the first time in my life. It has been surprisingly fulfilling. Following the science: Studies have found that expressing gratitude, particularly through writing , can improve our sense of well-being.\n\n 💡 How I did it: I made a list of artists whose songs, shows and films have brought me joy.\n\n Early entries included Barbra Streisand, Richard Carpenter (one half of the '70s singing duo the Carpenters), Tina Fey and Andrew Scott (the actor best known for playing the \"hot priest\" in \"Fleabag\"). I bought a fresh pack of envelopes and a new sheet of stamps and got to work. I've tried to send a letter every couple of weeks, usually to agents or management offices.\n\n When I sit down to write, I think about the ways each artist has added color to my life. I reflect on the times they made me smile, laugh, cry or sing along. It's been a lovely way to spend my time. 💌 Reality check: I know my thank-you notes may never reach their intended recipients — and even if they do, the odds of getting any replies are very low.\n\n But the process has been its own reward. Share this story ... Get Axios Nashville ... Find your Axios Local city . \n\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\nA MESSAGE FROM AMAZON\r\n\n \r\n Amazon supports American communities and small businesses \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n Amazon has invested more than $1.8 trillion in the U.S., through infrastructure and compensation to employees since 2010.\n\n\r\n The impact: Amazon is investing in communities across America, helping employees and whole communities thrive.\n\n\r\n Learn about Amazon’s economic impact in your community. \n\n\r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n 2. 🏛️ Parting shot! \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n Photo: J. David Ake/Getty Images November's full moon — known as the Beaver Moon — rising behind the tip of the Washington Monument last night.\n\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n 🏁 Please invite your friends to join Finish Line . \n\n \r\n 👆 Like this comms style and format? It's called Smart Brevity®. Bring it to your org — via hands-on training or internal comms software — to harness its power and impact. \r\n &nbsp; Axios thanks our partners for supporting our journalism.\n Advertise with us. \n\n Read more about Axios' mission , ethics and how we use AI in our journalism . You can reach the authors by replying to this email.\nSponsorship has no influence on editorial content.\n\n Thank you for signing up for this Axios newsletter. To stop receiving this newsletter, unsubscribe or manage your email preferences . If someone forwarded this to you, sign up now to get Axios in your inbox.\n\n Axios, PO Box 101060, Arlington VA 22201 &nbsp; Follow Axios across:\n\n &nbsp; &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;",
